Process log source attribution

The invocation log binding follows confctl's Logger, LineBuffer and command
owners in lib/confctl/logger.rb, lib/confctl/line_buffer.rb,
lib/confctl/cli/log_view.rb, lib/confctl/cli/command.rb and
lib/confctl/system_command.rb. Those project sources retain the repository's
GPL-3.0 license; this notice does not replace LICENSE.txt.

Command start/chunk/exit presentation and ordering were adapted with reference
to tty-command 0.10.1, by Piotr Murach:
lib/tty/command.rb; lib/tty/command/cmd.rb;
lib/tty/command/process_runner.rb; lib/tty/command/exit_error.rb;
lib/tty/command/truncator.rb; lib/tty/command/child_process.rb;
lib/tty/command/printers/abstract.rb; lib/tty/command/printers/pretty.rb.

The Go binding keeps literal arguments and its existing owned Start/Wait/group
cancellation, full byte captures and trim-one-LF presentation. It streams each
captured chunk once, skips the summary after infrastructure failure, and treats
callback errno/EOF as failure rather than Ruby's broad read-stream rescue.
Metadata bypasses live readers and Flush. Native file Flush is a no-op, without
buffering or fsync. These are explicit port differences, not native parity.

